{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"archive|derived view|turn\" docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md'","aggregated_output":"35:The platform also preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\n36:history at low-level entry grain, from which turns, chunks, summaries, and\n72:tools, artifacts, sources, archive, and review.\n84:| Archive | Fastify + Convex + cache/index layers | Full-fidelity low-level process history, turn derivation, later chunk/view derivation inputs | Processes | Canonical history is preserved at entry grain; turns and chunks are derived over it |\n171:| Full-fidelity archive entries are canonical while turns are derived | Context-management features can evolve without rewriting the archive |\n172:| Chunks summarize turns instead of replacing them | Derived views remain rebuildable from the archive |\n285:**Choice:** The platform preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\n293:**Consequence:** The archive is append-oriented and durable. It is not the same\n299:**Choice:** The canonical archive stores the following finalized low-level entry\n311:for later turn-level querying, tool-call management, summarization, fidelity\n314:differently without overfitting the archive to provider-specific wire shapes.\n317:`model_turn` or `artifact_event` layer at this stage. More specific process\n323:to the canonical archive. Only finalized/completed entries are appended.\n326:the durable archive should remain queryable, stable, and semantically useful\n327:for later turn/chunk derivation and long-horizon context management.\n335:**Choice:** `Turn` is the primary grouping derived from archived entries.\n336:`Chunk` is a later derived grouping over one or more turns.\n338:**Rationale:** A turn is the most legible human and process unit for querying\n340:strategies, so chunking should not be baked into the archive grain.\n342:**Consequence:** Archive entries carry the information needed to derive turns.\n446:without turning the frontend into a separate application server model.\n576:  already-grouped turns or already-compressed summaries as canonical history.\n626:- Exact delegated-process history capture, turn-derivation metadata, and\n695:- canonical archive thinking\n698:- archive vs derived-view separation\n710:- the overall platform architecture; reuse the archive/projection ideas, not the\n844:- [ ] Canonical archive entry taxonomy and finalized-entry rule are explicit\n845:- [ ] Turns and later chunks are clearly derived over archived entries\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
