s'];\n   303\t        getProcessEnvironmentProviderKind: PlatformStore['getProcessEnvironmentProviderKind'];\n   304\t        getProcessEnvironmentSummary: PlatformStore['getProcessEnvironmentSummary'];\n   305\t        getProcessWorkingSetFingerprint: PlatformStore['getProcessWorkingSetFingerprint'];\n   306\t        listProcessOutputs: PlatformStore['listProcessOutputs'];\n   307\t        listProjectArtifacts: PlatformStore['listProjectArtifacts'];\n   308\t        listProjectProcesses: PlatformStore['listProjectProcesses'];\n   309\t        listProjectSourceAttachments: PlatformStore['listProjectSourceAttachments'];\n   310\t        setProcessHydrationPlan: PlatformStore['setProcessHydrationPlan'];\n   311\t        upsertProcessEnvironmentState: PlatformStore['upsertProcessEnvironmentState'];\n   312\t      },\n   313\t      gitHubRepositoryResolver,\n   314\t      new RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor(\n   315\t        platformStore,\n   316\t        providerAdapterRegistry,\n   317\t        env.DEFAULT_ENVIRONMENT_PROVIDER_KIND,\n   318\t      ),\n   319\t    );\n   320\t  const sourceProvenanceService =\n   321\t    options.sourceProvenanceService ??\n   322\t    new DefaultSourceProvenanceService(\n   323\t      platformStore as PlatformStore & {\n   324\t        createSourceProvenance: NonNullable<PlatformStore['createSourceProvenance']>;\n   325\t        getCurrentProcessMaterialRefs: NonNullable<PlatformStore['getCurrentProcessMaterialRefs']>;\n   326\t        listProcessSourceProvenance: NonNullable<PlatformStore['listProcessSourceProvenance']>;\n   327\t      },\n   328\t      sourceRefreshService,\n   329\t    );\n   330\t  const processEnvironmentService =\n   331\t    options.processEnvironmentService ??\n   332\t    new ProcessEnvironmentService(\n   333\t      platformStore,\n   334\t      processAccessService,\n   335\t      providerAdapterRegistry,\n   336\t      processLiveHub,\n   337\t      scriptExecutionService,\n   338\t      checkpointPlanner,\n   339\t      codeCheckpointWriter,\n   340\t      env.DEFAULT_ENVIRONMENT_PROVIDER_KIND,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Canonical archive append/read, turn derivation, derived-view routes, and client surfaces are implemented end to end, and both `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed.\",\"The degraded-state story is inconsistent across surfaces: archive-entry degradation is computed in the archive read service, but turn and derived-view rebuilds read raw archive rows and can report the same process slice as `ready`.\",\"The deferred finalization path is not lossless. Under partial artifact/provenance failure it can drop finalized entries entirely, which breaks reopen consistency and any later turn/view derivation that depends on the archive as canonical truth.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ArchiveReadService` bypasses the existing source-provenance read service and rehydrates source provenance from raw store rows, so archive-source coherence can drift from the rest of the source domain.\",\"Flow 7 in the tech design says archive, turns, and derived views use cursor-bounded reads; derived views currently implement only a hard `slice(0, 50)` with no cursor/query contract.\",\"The production runtime still exercises archive finalization through the shared default placeholder script payload rather than process-type-specific execution logic.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Happy-path coverage is strong: durable archive tables, archive routes, turn rebuilds, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and client rendering are all present and exercised by passing tests.\",\"Coverage is weak for degraded reopen scenarios. The existing suites assert missing-record degradation on archive reads, but they do not catch deferred-entry loss, turn/view degradation drift, or source-detach/access-revocation behavior after reopen.\",\"Epic 7 is close on the happy path, but the current implementation does not fully preserve the 'archive stays visible and projections degrade locally' contract under partial-failure conditions.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"I did not find the in-memory provider fake wired into production; the material non-real path is the real runtime default in `ScriptExecutionService`, which still emits a canned 'default execution payload'.\",\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` has a lossy production branch: unresolved artifact/source bindings cause the code to skip the finalized entry instead of persisting a degraded canonical row.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when related artifact or source provenance cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` resolves `artifactCheckpointIndex` / `sourceProvenanceBinding` and then `continue`s when either lookup is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts` lines 783-810). That drops finalized deferred entries instead of appending a degraded archive row, violating the archive-truth requirement when checkpoint/provenance side effects partially fail.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view rebuilds ignore related-context degradation computed by archive reads\",\"evidence\":\"`TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` pages raw archive rows from `platformStore.listArchiveEntries` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts` lines 48-50 and 89-111) and only degrades turns when the stored row already has `entryStatus === 'degraded'` (lines 149-154). Missing artifact/source context is added later by `ArchiveReadService` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 163-224), so turns and derived views can stay `ready` while the archive page shows degraded entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive reopen bypasses source-provenance degradation logic for detached or revoked sources\",\"evidence\":\"`ArchiveReadService` loads raw `StoredSourceProvenanceRecord` rows and copies their stored `entryStatus` / `degradationReason` directly into archive responses (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 120-125 and 198-212). The actual read-time degradation logic for detached/redacted/unavailable sources lives in `DefaultSourceProvenanceService.listProcessSourceProvenance` / `buildSourceProvenanceEntry` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts` lines 153-199 and 223-285). A source that later detaches or loses access will still read as `ready` in the archive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-004\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Derived-view reads are bounded but not cursor-paginated as designed\",\"evidence\":\"Flow 7 says archive entries, turns, and derived views use cursor pagination with default limits (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md` lines 668-674). The derived-view route schema has no querystring contract (`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` lines 37-46), and the service simply `slice(0, 50)`s the computed set (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts` lines 210-211).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-005\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production execution still runs through a placeholder default script payload\",\"evidence\":\"`ScriptExecutionService` builds a canned 'default execution payload' with fixed artifact/tool/archive output text (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts` lines 15-18 and 52-60), placeholder side-work summaries (`lines 233-236`), and an explicit comment that process-type-specific payloads 'come later' (`lines 279-283`). This is a real runtime default, not just test infrastructure.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but `guard:no-test-changes` currently prints `SKIP`, so the story gate's extra protection is scaffolded rather than enforced.\",\"Whether the placeholder default execution payload is accepted temporary debt outside Epic 7 needs an explicit product/architecture ruling before treating the archive path as production-real.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
