{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-7 are wired end-to-end through shared contracts, Convex tables, Fastify routes, and client archive surfaces, and both requested verification gates succeeded.\",\"The cross-story happy path works, but the execution-to-archive handoff still breaks canonical-truth guarantees in two places: production runs emit placeholder archive content, and deferred entries are dropped instead of downgraded when provenance/checkpoint resolution fails.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The archive storage/read architecture is coherent, but the execution boundary drifts from the tech design: `createApp` composes a real provider registry while `ScriptExecutionService` still defaults to a canned payload instead of a process-specific runtime.\",\"Turn and derived-view GET reads rebuild projections on every request rather than primarily serving cached projections, which weakens the bounded-read strategy described in the tech design for long histories.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Implemented coverage is strong on the green path: archive persistence, archive APIs, turn derivation, derived-view responses, and provenance enrichment all shipped and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` plus `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both succeeded.\",\"Coverage is incomplete on degraded production behavior: there is no protection against losing deferred canonical entries when artifact/source linkage cannot be resolved at append time.\",\"The epic gate passed, but the `test:e2e` leg is still scaffold-only, so no executable browser/runtime end-to-end archive scenario is currently enforced by automation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The in-memory/failing provider adapters and stub checkpoint writer are clearly test-only seams and are not the material concern.\",\"The material non-real production path is `ScriptExecutionService`'s default payload, which fabricates a `Default Execution Summary`, canned reasoning/tool/model/process archive entries, and a dummy source checkpoint note for writable repos.\",\"When deferred archive entries depend on artifact or source provenance, the production orchestrator currently skips the entry entirely if that relation cannot be resolved, creating a missing-history path instead of a degraded-but-readable canonical archive record.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Production executions still archive placeholder output instead of real process work\",\"evidence\":\"The production composition root instantiates `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` with no custom payload factory (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`), so runtime execution falls back to `buildDefaultScriptPayload`. That default script writes a `Default Execution Summary`, emits canned `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries, and stages a dummy writable-source file with commit message `Record default execution note` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-317`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when provenance or checkpoint relations cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"The orchestrator defers entries with `artifactCheckpointIndex` or `sourceProvenanceBinding`, but `appendDeferredArchiveEntries` uses `continue` when the related artifact version or source provenance record is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:783-810`). A direct repro against that helper returned `{\\\"entries\\\":[],\\\"page\\\":{\\\"cursor\\\":null,\\\"nextCursor\\\":null,\\\"hasMore\\\":false}}` after attempting to append a deferred `script_emission` entry with unresolved relations, so canonical history is lost instead of surfaced as degraded metadata.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the intended cache-first bounded-read design\",\"evidence\":\"Every `GET /archive/turns` request forces `rebuildTurns` before listing turns (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `GET /archive/derived-views` likewise rebuilds turns and rewrites stored views on read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-75`). This preserves correctness today but adds avoidable full-archive work and write amplification on normal reads.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether the placeholder execution payload is an explicit temporary stopgap or an unintended leftover from Epic 3; either way it should not ship as canonical archive truth.\",\"No executable e2e suite currently verifies the browser/runtime archive flow because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
